Subject: Kaplan Meier - confidence interval for the median
Message-ID: <0A30918CCACC564BB94202B4DD7C8B2C01C2A2B3@SPOTEXVS02.corp.cvt.int>

 I'd like to find out whether or not the method, used in SPLUS,  for computing the confidence interval for the median of a Kaplan Meier estimate is the method of

Brookmeyer, Crowley, “A confidence Interval for the Median Survival Time”, Biometrics, 38, 29-41, 1982.

 Interestingly, for the simple dataset of , (10, 15, 23, 30, 35, 52, 100+) (and + indicates censoring)

 SPLUS gives, the median and CI as 30 (15, NA), (R reports the upper limit as inf) 

 while SAS gives 30 (15,52)

